✅ 4. Where to safely open the evaluation file

Replace this line:

Set evalWB = Workbooks.Open(evalFolder & evalfile, ReadOnly:=True)

✅ WITH THIS (right before opening the file)

If Dir(evalFolder & evalFileName) = "" Then GoTo NextFile
Set evalWB = Workbooks.Open(evalFolder & evalFileName, ReadOnly:=True)


---

✅ 5. Where to release the workbook before moving

Every time you close the evaluation file, add these lines right after:

🔧 BEFORE

evalWB.Close SaveChanges:=False
file.Move completedFolder & evalfile

✅ AFTER

evalWB.Close SaveChanges:=False
Set evalWB = Nothing
DoEvents

file.Move completedFolder & evalFileName

📌 Apply this same pattern to Completed and Invalid moves.


---

✅ 6. Where to fix the false “File updated successfully”

This is in ValidatePaths, not the main macro.

🔧 REPLACE THIS:

On Error GoTo CleanExit
UpdateSupplierEvaluationSummary

✅ WITH THIS:

On Error GoTo ErrHandler
UpdateSupplierEvaluationSummary
GoTo CleanExit

ErrHandler:
    MsgBox "Process ended with error: " & Err.Description, vbCritical
    Exit Sub

✔️ Now success only shows if no error happened


